1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,777
Karenai

2
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:35,840
Let's go.

3
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:42,398
I'll be right back.

4
00:01:50,960 --> 00:01:51,790
There.

5
00:01:52,060 --> 00:01:53,060
Now I'm ready.

6
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:57,220
Alright, kid.

7
00:01:57,500 --> 00:02:01,420
Before we get into it, there's
something I want to ask you.

8
00:02:01,940 --> 00:02:02,770
What?

9
00:02:04,960 --> 00:02:09,280
You didn't, you know, kill Vice
Commander Fanatio, did you?

10
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:11,020
She's alive.

11
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:14,240
She's being healed as we speak.

12
00:02:16,060 --> 00:02:16,940
That's good.

13
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:21,300
Since you spared her life, I'll
return the favor and spare yours.

14
00:02:23,300 --> 00:02:24,500
How disrespectful.

15
00:02:26,760 --> 00:02:28,120
Why do you think that?

16
00:02:29,020 --> 00:02:31,373
If you're this high up in the Cathedral,

17
00:02:31,640 --> 00:02:34,640
you must be the commander
of the Integrity Knights.

18
00:02:34,980 --> 00:02:35,810
Yeah?

19
00:02:35,893 --> 00:02:36,860
What if I am?

20
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:39,080
What about the others?

21
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:41,165
Fanatio isn't the only knight.

22
00:02:42,580 --> 00:02:45,520
Eldrie, the four Whirling Blades, Alice.

23
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:47,300
What about them?

24
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:48,539
Don't they matter?

25
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:49,880
I see.

26
00:02:50,180 --> 00:02:51,592
You're taking that road.

27
00:02:52,220 --> 00:02:53,820
How do I put this?

28
00:02:54,380 --> 00:02:56,086
Eldrie is Alice's apprentice.

29
00:02:56,540 --> 00:03:02,480
The four Whirling Blades, Dakira, Jace,
Holvren, and Jiro, they're Fanatios.

30
00:03:03,020 --> 00:03:03,960
And her?

31
00:03:04,300 --> 00:03:06,535
Well, she happens to be my apprentice.

32
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:09,497
It's not that I don't
care about the others.

33
00:03:09,580 --> 00:03:12,900
It's just, I'm invested in Fanatio.

34
00:03:13,320 --> 00:03:16,791
That's why if you killed her,
I'd be obliged to avenge her.

35
00:03:17,060 --> 00:03:18,740
That's all there is to it.

36
00:03:20,260 --> 00:03:22,260
Though, now that I think about it,

37
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:25,576
I guess little Alice does
look up to me as her mentor.

38
00:03:26,100 --> 00:03:28,517
She's not the same as
she was six years ago,

39
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:31,129
when she first became
an apprentice knight.

40
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:35,840
If me and her went at it now, I
don't know who'd come out on top.

41
00:03:38,800 --> 00:03:41,437
Anyway, seeing as how
Alice is as strong as me,

42
00:03:41,520 --> 00:03:43,696
you must have snuck past her somehow.

43
00:03:43,920 --> 00:03:46,180
But you won't be so lucky with me.

44
00:03:47,140 --> 00:03:49,937
Come to think of it,
shouldn't there be two of you?

45
00:03:50,020 --> 00:03:52,460
The Prime Senator said you had a partner.

46
00:03:53,060 --> 00:03:55,100
I guess if he's not here with you,

47
00:03:55,300 --> 00:03:58,594
that means he's off somewhere
keeping little Alice busy.

48
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:01,540
Yeah, he probably is.

49
00:04:02,560 --> 00:04:03,420
I'm ready.

50
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:05,357
Let's get this over with.

51
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:08,000
I'm curious to see who will avenge you.

52
00:04:09,700 --> 00:04:10,880
No one, kid.

53
00:04:11,260 --> 00:04:12,960
I don't have a mentor.

54
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:25,500
Norkia style.

55
00:04:25,820 --> 00:04:26,800
Lightning Slash.

56
00:04:27,060 --> 00:04:29,140
Or it's something like it.

57
00:04:29,460 --> 00:04:31,020
With his sword like that,

58
00:04:31,220 --> 00:04:34,867
it'll take him an extra move or
two to activate the technique.

59
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:39,700
But if I use the Aincrad-style
Sonic Leap, I can strike him first.

60
00:04:41,880 --> 00:04:44,056
Ah, now that's an interesting stance.

61
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:46,129
I've never seen it before.

62
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:48,000
Do you use combo attacks?

63
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:50,340
Maybe I do.

64
00:04:50,580 --> 00:04:51,600
Maybe I don't.

65
00:04:51,760 --> 00:04:52,780
Why do you care?

66
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:54,160
I don't.

67
00:04:54,380 --> 00:04:59,197
It's just that there was a knight from the
Dark Territory who liked to use him, too.

68
00:04:59,280 --> 00:05:01,515
I fought him a couple of times before.

69
00:05:01,700 --> 00:05:04,440
I didn't like the
experience, to be honest.

70
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:06,500
My style's simple.

71
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:10,120
Doing all them flashy moves
is way too complicated.

72
00:05:10,600 --> 00:05:11,600
Is that so?

73
00:05:11,860 --> 00:05:13,897
Do you want me to fight like you then?

74
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:17,180
Using only conventional moves? Hell no.

75
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:18,997
You want to use combo attacks?

76
00:05:19,080 --> 00:05:19,910
Go ahead.

77
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:22,620
I can handle anything you dish out, kid.

78
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:25,057
I should warn you, though.

79
00:05:25,140 --> 00:05:29,600
I'm going to use my best move
first, and you ain't ready for it.

80
00:05:32,320 --> 00:05:37,000
If his sword's already in perfect
control, then I've only got one chance.

81
00:05:37,380 --> 00:05:41,340
As he activates his move,
I'll attack with Sonic Leap.

82
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:45,400
Taste the blade of Bercouli Synthesis 1.

83
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:49,740
On guard! Bercouli?

84
00:06:03,860 --> 00:06:06,280
That ripple, it's where he just slashed.

85
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:26,940
Oof, talk about cutting it close.

86
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:31,934
The last thing I expected was for you
to come rushing in at me like that.

87
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:33,520
Sorry, kid.

88
00:06:33,880 --> 00:06:35,540
I damn near killed you.

89
00:06:36,220 --> 00:06:38,180
Yeah, I know you did.

90
00:06:38,420 --> 00:06:39,420
But with what?

91
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:43,400
That was my best move,
just like I told you.

92
00:06:43,940 --> 00:06:47,277
When I took that swing, I
wasn't just slicing air.

93
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:51,380
I was slicing a moment in
the future, so to speak.

94
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:53,700
Slicing the future?

95
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:58,097
The first time I saw a Dark
Knight use a combo attack

96
00:06:58,180 --> 00:07:01,680
was just after I became an
Integrity Knight myself.

97
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:05,577
The sword techniques I
learned were all about putting

98
00:07:05,660 --> 00:07:08,720
as much strength as I could
behind a single strike.

99
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:12,597
But sword techniques using
combination moves focus

100
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:15,940
on how to handle your enemy's
attacks and land hits.

101
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:20,640
It's pretty obvious which is
more practical than a fight.

102
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:24,600
Anyway, I got beat up
real good, but I survived.

103
00:07:25,260 --> 00:07:29,400
Then I got to thinking how I could
land a hit against a combo user.

104
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:33,280
I found the answer with this thing.

105
00:07:34,440 --> 00:07:38,020
Originally, it was part of a
divine object called a clock.

106
00:07:38,380 --> 00:07:41,498
It used to hang on the wall
of the central cathedral.

107
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:46,440
It was here when the world was
first created, or so I was told.

108
00:07:48,420 --> 00:07:50,180
It had a weird name.

109
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:54,089
The Pontifex called it System
Clock, or something like that.

110
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:57,089
When little Alice uses
her Osmanthus blade,

111
00:07:57,360 --> 00:08:00,080
it cuts through the
horizontal axis of space.

112
00:08:00,540 --> 00:08:03,680
But mine cuts the vertical axis of time.

113
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:08,540
Now it's got a new name,
the Time-Splitting Sword.

114
00:08:09,880 --> 00:08:13,400
When he swung it, the force
of his strike stayed in place.

115
00:08:13,760 --> 00:08:16,936
That means I don't have a
chance against him up close.

116
00:08:17,900 --> 00:08:20,018
I'll have to use long-range attacks.

117
00:08:20,880 --> 00:08:21,820
System call.

118
00:08:22,220 --> 00:08:23,177
Connect armament.

119
00:08:23,260 --> 00:08:24,090
Search archive...

120
00:08:24,173 --> 00:08:28,453
Let me guess, you're setting yourself
up to attack from a distance, right?

121
00:08:28,540 --> 00:08:30,580
Everyone who sees that move does.

122
00:08:31,720 --> 00:08:35,137
Same goals for all the Integrity
Knights that came after me,

123
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:37,120
including Fanatio and Alice.

124
00:08:37,820 --> 00:08:40,417
Once they saw that move,
they picked long-range,

125
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:42,853
perfect control to try and deal with it.

126
00:08:43,140 --> 00:08:44,258
I can't blame them.

127
00:08:44,880 --> 00:08:48,704
Trying to bring me down got to be
sort of a contest between them.

128
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,560
But I never lost.

129
00:08:50,840 --> 00:08:54,664
I sparred with all of them, and
here I am, still their commander.

130
00:08:57,640 --> 00:09:01,980
Well, if one of them does take
my job, it'll probably be Alice.

131
00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:05,377
I sure am looking forward to this, though.

132
00:09:05,460 --> 00:09:10,380
I'm curious to see what kind of moves
helped you get past all those nights?

133
00:09:11,320 --> 00:09:13,180
Don't worry you will!

134
00:09:15,760 --> 00:09:21,160
Come and get it kid this
time I won't go easy on you.

135
00:09:41,380 --> 00:09:42,780
Let's go.

136
00:10:15,260 --> 00:10:16,660
Clever.

137
00:10:20,140 --> 00:10:22,277
Blue Rose Sword.

138
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:24,397
Lend me your power!

139
00:10:24,480 --> 00:10:27,040
Release Recollection?

140
00:10:33,580 --> 00:10:35,440
Now pay close attention.

141
00:10:35,880 --> 00:10:40,640
The perfect weapon control art has
two stages, enhance and release.

142
00:10:41,640 --> 00:10:43,400
Enhance? Release?

143
00:10:44,720 --> 00:10:48,580
Yes, enhancing awakens part
of your weapon's memories.

144
00:10:48,980 --> 00:10:51,680
The act causes a new attack to manifest.

145
00:10:52,140 --> 00:10:56,317
In the releasing stage, you can
awaken all of your weapon's memories.

146
00:10:56,400 --> 00:10:59,380
Then you can unleash
its most savage power.

147
00:10:59,760 --> 00:11:01,320
Oh, I get it.

148
00:11:07,220 --> 00:11:09,200
That explains Eldrie's win.

149
00:11:09,540 --> 00:11:13,599
In its enhanced stage, it can get
longer than normal, and then split.

150
00:11:18,420 --> 00:11:21,860
Then its release stage was
when it changed into a snake.

151
00:11:22,300 --> 00:11:23,217
You are correct.

152
00:11:23,300 --> 00:11:27,540
That said, you too should avoid
using release for the time being.

153
00:11:28,300 --> 00:11:29,440
Why should we?

154
00:11:29,780 --> 00:11:31,721
Because you are not yet ready to.

155
00:11:31,920 --> 00:11:34,155
You have only just learned of the art.

156
00:11:34,380 --> 00:11:35,780
Until you master it,

157
00:11:35,920 --> 00:11:39,744
you cannot control the power
generated by your weapon's memories.

158
00:11:40,180 --> 00:11:42,945
Especially those of a
divine object like yours.

159
00:11:43,260 --> 00:11:46,000
It can harm you as much as your enemy.

160
00:11:46,620 --> 00:11:49,560
If you're not careful, it will kill you.

161
00:11:59,840 --> 00:12:03,920
I never saw a swordsman toss
his blade during a fight before.

162
00:12:04,440 --> 00:12:06,852
Did you come up with that trick yourself?

163
00:12:07,240 --> 00:12:08,070
Uh-uh.

164
00:12:08,153 --> 00:12:10,020
My partner taught me that one.

165
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:12,980
The battlefield has lots of opportunities.

166
00:12:13,360 --> 00:12:15,419
Anything can be a weapon or a trap.

167
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,540
Make the best of what you got. Smart.

168
00:12:20,120 --> 00:12:23,296
Well, you might have gotten
the upper hand this round,

169
00:12:23,540 --> 00:12:26,400
but there's no way in
hell you're gonna beat me!

170
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:45,197
The Blue Rose Sword has two dormant
memories, Eternal Ice and Rose.

171
00:12:45,280 --> 00:12:49,920
When I activate Eternal
Ice, it freezes everything.

172
00:12:50,580 --> 00:12:52,660
Now I'll show you what Rose can do.

173
00:12:54,820 --> 00:12:56,520
Blue Rose Bloom!

174
00:13:02,160 --> 00:13:03,220
What'd you do?

175
00:13:03,440 --> 00:13:07,680
The Rose's bloom by absorbing the
life of those trapped in the ice.

176
00:13:09,820 --> 00:13:11,680
Goddammit, you little punk.

177
00:13:12,540 --> 00:13:15,797
So is this your plan all
along, killing the both of us?

178
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:17,700
Not us, just you.

179
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:21,720
You have an advantage over
me in every way except one.

180
00:13:22,360 --> 00:13:24,600
It's your total amount of life left.

181
00:13:25,060 --> 00:13:29,340
Based on your appearance, you became
an Integrity Knight in your 40s.

182
00:13:29,780 --> 00:13:33,020
So, your life value is lower than mine.

183
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:37,140
I'm younger and my life
value is near its peak.

184
00:13:37,700 --> 00:13:42,620
Even though you landed a hit, the life
I have left is still higher than yours.

185
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:44,548
That's what I hoped anyway.

186
00:13:45,040 --> 00:13:47,820
Kid, you don't know what
you're talking about.

187
00:13:48,340 --> 00:13:51,380
You just said I became
an Integrity Knight.

188
00:13:52,140 --> 00:13:53,905
A knight's all I've ever been.

189
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:56,197
I didn't have a life
before I was summoned.

190
00:13:56,280 --> 00:13:59,515
And that's the part of you
people I find so despicable.

191
00:13:59,940 --> 00:14:02,058
You've forgotten who you used to be.

192
00:14:02,160 --> 00:14:06,097
You're loyal to the Axiom Church
without knowing what it really is.

193
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:10,180
You act like you're champions of
justice, but you uphold corruption.

194
00:14:11,140 --> 00:14:14,557
You think you're here because the
Pontifex summoned you from heaven,

195
00:14:14,640 --> 00:14:15,740
but that's a lie.

196
00:14:16,560 --> 00:14:18,040
You had a mother.

197
00:14:18,460 --> 00:14:20,477
She's the one who gave
you the name Bercouli.

198
00:14:20,560 --> 00:14:22,460
You're human, just like me.

199
00:14:25,040 --> 00:14:25,870
Bercouli.

200
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:29,940
In my village, they tell stories
about how much of a hero you were.

201
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:32,720
What stories?

202
00:14:33,780 --> 00:14:34,697
Think back.

203
00:14:34,780 --> 00:14:37,074
I'm sure you've seen this sword before.

204
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:41,840
Yeah, I have. Somewhere.

205
00:14:42,980 --> 00:14:43,810
Right.

206
00:14:43,940 --> 00:14:44,920
Years ago.

207
00:14:45,540 --> 00:14:48,200
It was in the nest of the white dragon.

208
00:14:48,580 --> 00:14:51,100
I saw it there after I killed it.

209
00:14:51,500 --> 00:14:53,180
You killed the dragon?

210
00:14:54,260 --> 00:14:55,880
I saw its bones.

211
00:14:57,320 --> 00:14:58,597
And now...

212
00:14:58,680 --> 00:15:02,217
Now you say the one who killed it was you.

213
00:15:02,300 --> 00:15:05,400
A dragon that protected the human realm.

214
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:07,560
The one from your own legend.

215
00:15:08,040 --> 00:15:10,800
Don't you remember
anything about your past?

216
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:12,460
About who you were?

217
00:15:13,220 --> 00:15:18,660
In Rulid, the village you founded and
where I was born, everyone knew about you.

218
00:15:19,220 --> 00:15:21,808
Young or old, we looked
up to you as a hero.

219
00:15:21,920 --> 00:15:24,560
But the Pontifex sealed
away your memories.

220
00:15:25,040 --> 00:15:28,760
She turned you into the
first Integrity Knight.

221
00:15:29,480 --> 00:15:30,757
Then came the others.

222
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:35,080
Everyone from Fanatio
to Eldrie, even Alice.

223
00:15:36,040 --> 00:15:37,100
All of you.

224
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:42,360
Before you became Integrity
Knights, you had lives.

225
00:15:42,700 --> 00:15:43,720
You were human.

226
00:15:44,880 --> 00:15:47,600
Sealed away my memories?

227
00:15:48,640 --> 00:15:53,400
I can't just believe a
wild story like that.

228
00:15:54,440 --> 00:16:01,297
But all that stuff I was told about
me being summoned from heaven And...

229
00:16:01,380 --> 00:16:03,617
I had my doubts...

230
00:16:03,700 --> 00:16:05,220
for a while now.

231
00:16:22,780 --> 00:16:23,880
Well, well.

232
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:26,200
Now, what do we have here?

233
00:16:33,280 --> 00:16:35,560
This won't do. No, no, no.

234
00:16:35,680 --> 00:16:38,500
This won't do at all, my dear commander.

235
00:16:39,500 --> 00:16:42,900
Surely, good sir, you don't
plan to die on us like this.

236
00:16:43,820 --> 00:16:48,740
That would be treason against her
eminence, the lovely Pontifex.

237
00:16:49,060 --> 00:16:52,920
If she were awake to see you in
this state, she would be livid.

238
00:16:53,740 --> 00:16:59,420
Prime Senator Judalkin, this
is a fight between swordsmen.

239
00:16:59,700 --> 00:17:03,320
A pig like you has no business here.

240
00:17:05,620 --> 00:17:08,300
After going so easy on this heretic,

241
00:17:08,580 --> 00:17:12,380
you have no business
correcting me, dear Commander.

242
00:17:13,160 --> 00:17:16,700
Pray tell, why did you not
use your sword's full power?

243
00:17:16,940 --> 00:17:17,820
If you had,

244
00:17:17,940 --> 00:17:20,057
you could have slaughtered
this loathsome brat

245
00:17:20,140 --> 00:17:22,417
before he opened his
slanderous little mouth.

246
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:27,517
God, you did not, and therefore committed
treason against the glorious pontifics.

247
00:17:27,600 --> 00:17:28,541
Shut your mouth.

248
00:17:29,540 --> 00:17:33,160
I fought with everything I had.

249
00:17:34,560 --> 00:17:36,300
But you lied to me.

250
00:17:37,340 --> 00:17:39,020
You lied to all of us.

251
00:17:40,140 --> 00:17:44,560
This kid ain't no assassin
from the Dark Territory.

252
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:50,317
And compared to an ugly piece
of shit like you... Silence!

253
00:17:50,400 --> 00:17:53,000
Be silent or I'll rip off your head!

254
00:17:54,920 --> 00:17:58,897
For your information, my dear,
we wouldn't have this problem?

255
00:17:58,980 --> 00:18:01,840
if you damned knights
weren't so damned useless.

256
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:07,457
Honestly, when her eminence awakes, you
knights will be thoroughly punished.

257
00:18:07,540 --> 00:18:12,380
At the very least, you and your precious
vice commander shall be reprocessed.

258
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:13,540
Re-what?

259
00:18:13,820 --> 00:18:16,020
You're talking out your ass again.

260
00:18:17,960 --> 00:18:19,157
System call!

261
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:20,600
Deep Freeze!

262
00:18:21,400 --> 00:18:24,940
Integrator Unit ID 001!

263
00:18:39,700 --> 00:18:44,640
We don't need old farts like Number
One stinking up the place anymore.

264
00:18:45,300 --> 00:18:48,277
Now we have a much younger, more useful...

265
00:18:48,360 --> 00:18:49,640
Kitty-tops.

266
00:18:51,200 --> 00:18:52,030
Alice.

267
00:18:55,300 --> 00:18:56,130
Eugeo.

268
00:18:56,520 --> 00:19:00,160
Is something the matter?
Huh? Oh, no. Nothing.

269
00:19:00,880 --> 00:19:05,097
As soon as the moon comes out, I think
we can start climbing up the wall again.

270
00:19:05,180 --> 00:19:09,004
Long as I can make spikes, it
should go pretty easy from here on.

271
00:19:09,560 --> 00:19:13,117
There's no minions above us, and
the others here ain't waking up.

272
00:19:13,200 --> 00:19:14,030
For now.

273
00:19:14,600 --> 00:19:18,659
Besides the lack of sacred power,
the only other big problem is food.

274
00:19:18,780 --> 00:19:21,057
I don't know about you, but I'm starving.

275
00:19:21,140 --> 00:19:24,957
If I think about how much further we
gotta go, my head starts spinning.

276
00:19:25,040 --> 00:19:28,500
Could you be any more of
a disappointment? What?

277
00:19:28,800 --> 00:19:31,917
Whether we miss a meal or two
is the least of our worries.

278
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,420
Unless you are a child.

279
00:19:33,860 --> 00:19:36,448
Yeah, well, technically,
I still sort of am.

280
00:19:36,680 --> 00:19:41,092
I might not act like it all the time,
but I'm not even out of my teens yet.

281
00:19:41,300 --> 00:19:42,877
I don't eat, my life goes down.

282
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:44,937
A problem you badass knights don't have.

283
00:19:45,020 --> 00:19:45,940
Such language.

284
00:19:46,640 --> 00:19:48,640
Even Integrity Knights get hungry.

285
00:19:48,800 --> 00:19:50,980
We must eat or we lose life like you.

286
00:19:55,700 --> 00:19:58,620
Whoa, hold on. Sorry. I was kidding.

287
00:19:59,220 --> 00:20:00,740
Of course you get hungry.

288
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:02,784
You're as alive as anyone else.

289
00:20:03,840 --> 00:20:06,546
Speaking of food, where
are Cardinal's snacks?

290
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:09,000
Oh, yeah.

291
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:10,697
I knew I snagged some more.

292
00:20:10,780 --> 00:20:11,610
Look it.

293
00:20:11,693 --> 00:20:12,523
It's dinner time.

294
00:20:14,160 --> 00:20:17,513
Why in the world would you
store your food in such a way?

295
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:19,510
I don't.

296
00:20:19,593 --> 00:20:21,197
I just tap my pocket and there they were.

297
00:20:21,280 --> 00:20:22,221
Try it sometime.

298
00:20:22,500 --> 00:20:24,971
But first, I gotta get these ready to eat.

299
00:20:28,220 --> 00:20:29,137
System call.

300
00:20:29,220 --> 00:20:30,691
Generate thermal element.

301
00:20:31,680 --> 00:20:32,510
Burst elements?

302
00:20:32,593 --> 00:20:34,080
Oh, you fool! What?

303
00:20:34,480 --> 00:20:36,940
If you use that art, you will burn them.

304
00:20:37,460 --> 00:20:38,290
Sorry.

305
00:20:43,160 --> 00:20:45,020
Generate thermal element.

306
00:20:45,740 --> 00:20:47,100
Aqueous element.

307
00:20:47,940 --> 00:20:48,822
Aerial element.

308
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:52,060
Vortex shape.

309
00:20:52,700 --> 00:20:53,540
Burst.

310
00:20:56,900 --> 00:20:57,740
Whoa.

311
00:20:58,520 --> 00:20:59,638
Hurry, give me one.

312
00:21:01,360 --> 00:21:03,760
Wait! No, no, no! I am joking.

313
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:12,480
That hit the spot.

314
00:21:12,960 --> 00:21:14,417
Thanks for showing me that.

315
00:21:14,500 --> 00:21:18,017
I didn't know you could steam food
using elements instead of a pan.

316
00:21:18,100 --> 00:21:20,197
Did you teach your little sis how to cook?

317
00:21:20,280 --> 00:21:22,162
Cause Selka's really good at it.

318
00:21:23,600 --> 00:21:25,360
What did you say just now?

319
00:21:28,160 --> 00:21:29,925
That you have a little sister?

320
00:21:30,680 --> 00:21:31,680
Her name's Selka.

321
00:21:32,840 --> 00:21:33,670
Sister.

322
00:21:39,820 --> 00:21:41,291
I can tell you about her.

323
00:21:42,420 --> 00:21:45,361
I can tell you everything
I know about this place.

324
00:21:46,040 --> 00:21:49,393
I don't know if you'll believe
me, but it's worth a shot.

325
00:21:52,440 --> 00:21:53,540
Go on, then.

326
00:21:55,520 --> 00:22:01,960
However, if I detect even a trace of deceit
in your words, I shall end your life.

327
00:22:41,300 --> 00:22:44,100
Thank you.

328
00:23:21,280 --> 00:23:23,997
Oh, oh,

329
00:23:24,080 --> 00:23:28,900
oh, oh, oh.

330
00:23:35,600 --> 00:23:38,240
Next time, Recollection.
